/*!
    \qmlmodule VSMM.Config
    \title VSMM.Config QML Module
    \brief User settings, saved to \c config.json.
*/

/*!
    \qmltype Config
    \nativetype vsmm::Config
    \inqmlmodule VSMM.Config
    \brief User settings, grouped into three value type sections.

    The settings are stored in \c config.json inside the application config
    location. Each section is a value type with real properties, and every
    member always has a value, so reads need no \c ?? guard.

    \qml
    Label { text: Config.paths.gameConfig }
    \endqml

    Assigning a member runs the setter of the whole section, then the change
    has to be saved:

    \qml
    Button {
        onClicked: {
            Config.paths.gameConfig = "/new/path"
            Config.saveToFile()
        }
    }
    \endqml

    Because every assignment goes through the section setter:
    \list
    \li Each assignment emits its own change signal, so setting two members
        of \c paths emits \c pathsChanged twice.
    \li Assigning an unchanged value does nothing and emits nothing.
    \endlist

    The destructor also saves, so values survive a clean shutdown without a
    \l saveToFile() call.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty generalSettings Config::general
    General behavior settings.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty pathSettings Config::paths
    Paths to the game data folder and the game executable.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty appearanceSettings Config::appearance
    Theme and accent color.
*/

/*!
    \qmlmethod void Config::saveToFile()
    Writes all three sections and the favorite mods to \c config.json.
    Changes to the sections are saved only by this call or at a clean
    shutdown. Favorite
    mods are the exception, they are saved as soon as they change.
*/

/*!
    \qmlvaluetype generalSettings
    \nativetype vsmm::GeneralSettings
    \inqmlmodule VSMM.Config
    \brief General behavior settings, the type of \l {Config::general}{Config.general}.

    Read a member directly, for example \c {Config.general.includeModPrerelease}.
    Assigning a member runs the setter of the whole section, which emits the
    section's change signal only when a value changed.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty bool generalSettings::deleteOldModVersion
    Move the old zip to the trash when a mod is updated, by a download or by
    loading a newer zip of a known mod with \l {ModLoader::load()}{ModLoader.load()}. A scan never deletes
    anything. Defaults to \c true.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty bool generalSettings::includeModPrerelease
    Consider pre-release versions when checking for updates. Defaults to
    \c false.
*/

/*!
    \qmlvaluetype pathSettings
    \nativetype vsmm::PathSettings
    \inqmlmodule VSMM.Config
    \brief Game paths, the type of \l {Config::paths}{Config.paths}.

    \l [QML] GameMngr reads both paths. Changing \l gameConfig makes it read the
    mods folders and disabled mods again, changing \l gameExe makes it read the
    game version again.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty string pathSettings::gameConfig
    The \c VintagestoryData folder. Empty by default.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty string pathSettings::gameExe
    The Vintage Story executable. Empty by default.
*/

/*!
    \qmlvaluetype appearanceSettings
    \nativetype vsmm::AppearanceSettings
    \inqmlmodule VSMM.Config
    \brief Look of the app, the type of \l {Config::appearance}{Config.appearance}.

    The backend only stores these values. The QML layer decides what the
    theme and accent index look like.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty enumeration appearanceSettings::theme
    The color theme. Defaults to \c Dark. Compare it with \c 0 or \c 1.

    \value Dark (0) Dark theme.
    \value Light (1) Light theme.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty int appearanceSettings::accentIndex
    Index of the accent color. Defaults to \c 0.
*/
